+# Tree/trash public projection contract blocker — 2026-11-12
+
+## Decision and scope
+
+Plan024 stage3 remains **pseudocode → sourcecode translation**, not new feature/API design. The bounded tree/readTrash unit was traced through Backend projection, public boundary and every production Mantine consumer. A concrete upstream-contract gap prevents a coherent consumer-preserving translation. The supervisor approved **documentation only**: do not add an unused Backend-only branch, change the public shape in isolation, omit slot/reference UI, invent a new envelope/read API or expose Backend internals to Mantine. No runtime or fixture bytes changed in this unit. This is not tree scope closure, stage3 completion or final acceptance.
+
+Authority remains Source45 > PlusCal25 > code138/stale. Full policy/plan/review003 and relevant Source/PlusCal were read before the decision. Existing WIP and untracked records were preserved. HEAD remains `28e6dc762c75c8a2ffbbe53ed08b323f0b2b82bd`. Exact pre-edit working bytes of the existing plan were snapshotted before editing; the incremental patch is not a diff against HEAD.
+
+## Specified procedures and branches
+
+| Authority | Required meaning and actual implementation/caller correspondence |
+| --- | --- |
+| `sourcescript/application/public_api/__init__.py:55-81,159-191`; `pseudocode/application/public_api/contract.pcal:39-44,136-166` (`InvokePublicHelper`) | `assets.readTree` and `assets.readTrash` are public Backend-query routes, not Application summaries. Explicit read arguments go to `dispatchProjectQuery`. Frontend uses official public methods, not Backend state/helpers. Every read is current, immutable/transient and not general mutation authority. Production `sourcecode/application/public_api/index.js:67-70` correctly queries readTree but binds readTrash to a separate summary wrapper. |
+| `sourcescript/backend/project_state.py:314-315,367-399` (`readBackendProjection(kind, request)`); `pseudocode/backend/project_state.pcal:563-583,659-710,735-740` (`BuildVfsRead(source,operation,request)`, `readBackendProjection(kind,request)`) | Capture current Backend source for this read; use registered operations; calculate detached canonical VFS tree from existing directories/assets. PlusCal builds directory nodes in existing order, appends CSV nodes in collection order, then image nodes in collection order, attaches by canonical parent path. readTree returns that tree; readTrash returns `TreeAtExactPath(tree,BackendSettings.defaults.vfs.trash)`. Common immutable return applies. No chart/slot summary is specified by these procedures. `sourcecode/backend/project_state.js:341-345` instead calls the flat summary helper; no official readTrash branch exists. This mismatch is established, not accepted as equivalent. |
+| `sourcescript/backend/assets_files.py:24-28,76-88,162-198,390-437`; `pseudocode/backend/project_state.pcal:583-612` | Canonical path comes from actual directory/name and segment boundaries, not a raw-prefix interpretation. `assets.isTrashed` uses descendant-or-same; `movable` requires current source existence and nonfixed directory, not non-trash membership. Selection resolves accepted/kind/path; draggable payload is detached kind/id/path/name only for existing non-trash CSV/image; directories/trash/absent return none. Move-options reject missing/fixed sources and directory descendants. Production `sourcecode/backend/project_state.js:299-315` and public query bindings already implement these neighboring reads; no gratuitous rewrite was made. |
+| `sourcescript/backend/project_state.py:319`; `sourcescript/backend/assets_files.py:461-481` (`collectAssetReferences(csvIds, imageIds, state)`); `pseudocode/backend/project_state.pcal:595-603` | Explicit-path deletion target resolves existing CSV/image, none for absent/directory. Return detached target, kind, canonical path, reference count and owners. Real project graph objects count separately even for repeated CSV; conversion rows are excluded; image counts per referring slot. Confirmation and cascade must use the same reference set. Backend `sourcecode/backend/project_state.js:324-333` supplies this per-asset read. Public `sourcecode/application/public_api/assets.js:111-117` instead takes current selected path with no explicit argument and reduces it to kind/id/path/name/count, dropping target/owners. Thus current public read cannot simply be used as an arbitrary-path owner/count replacement. |
+| `sourcescript/frontend/mantine_ui.py:19-38,112-119`; `pseudocode/frontend/mantine_ui.pcal:221-238` (`ProjectTreeAction(action,node,target)`) | Tree is a current VFS/assets projection, no independent authority. Trash CSV/image remain selectable; nonfixed trash sources can move out without implicit reference restore; move/menu converge on planMove/move. Slot connection is distinct, only non-trash CSV/image. UI-local modal confirmation target is permitted, but no concrete all-slot/chart summary or trash-count public calculation is defined. Actual calls are traced below, not silently removed. |
+| `sourcescript/application/public_api/assets.py:173-284`; `pseudocode/application/public_api/assets.pcal:146-207` | Delete/move/emptyTrash/createDirectory/connect remain commands with current revalidation and their distinct public returns. Existing move planning can provide one exact node/subtree count (`pseudocode/backend/assets_files.pcal:303-324`), but fixed-root move rejection means it is not an authorized generic trash-root summary API. Mutation input copies/plans are proposals, not read or commit authority. These mutation owners were not changed. |
+
+`DetachedDirectoryNodesInExistingOrder`, `AppendDetachedAssetTreeNode` and `AttachNodesByCanonicalParentPath` specify the canonical tree relationship/order, not a replacement all-chart/slot summary payload. A concrete JS/Mantine node representation can realize the specified relationship, but adding unspecified chart/slot/count fields or a wrapper envelope would choose additional public meaning. No such choice was made.
+
+## Current implementation shape and full actual-caller map
+
+`sourcecode/backend/assets_files.js:512-549` (`projectDataTreeSnapshot(objects = {})`) returns a flat record: directories; CSV id/name/path/readable/rowCount; image id/name/path; chart id/editable/csvIds/csvReferences; slot id/row/col/hidden/contentType/chart/imageId. `sourcecode/application/public_api/assets.js:64-72` (`projectDataTreeObjects()`) obtains files/data/images/charts/slots via `projectObjects.read`. Its `readProjectTrash()` at `sourcecode/application/public_api/assets.js:131-143` combines this flat snapshot with live reference counting and returns mutable `{hasContents,referenceCount}`, not the official immutable trash subtree. The official Backend readTree uses one current source and freezes its result, but its payload remains the wrong flat summary. Preserving freshness alone does not establish shape correspondence.
+
+Production search `readTree\(|readTrash\(|projectDataTreeObjects\(|projectDataTreeSnapshot\(` in `sourcecode` found the two public readTree consumers, one public readTrash consumer, the Backend helper call and Application trash helper call. Imports/public bindings were also inspected.
+
+| Actual caller | Values consumed and behavior that must not disappear |
+| --- | --- |
+| `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js:593-617,694-759` (`FastFigureProjectDataTree`) | Calls readTree each render; uses `.directories`, sorts them, builds directory→CSV→image Mantine rows from `.data`/`.images`, path-keyed revision/memo and metadata maps. CSV readability/row count, repeated chart CSV references and slot image counts come from the flat record, not a canonical tree alone. Canonical parent/path identity drives selection, row kind and drag handling. Existing sort order is implementation behavior, not the upstream collection-order contract. |
+| `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js:761-950` | Tree selection invokes selectDirectory/selectCsv/selectImage; movable and isTrashed remain public queries. Trash alone does not disable a row. Directory and asset menus use planMove/move, not a second mutation authority. Existing asset download and external directory import remain public calls. New tree rendering cannot break these identities or distinguish move versus connection by one uniform draggable flag. |
+| `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js:951-1004,1218-1275` | `/slots` displays every visible slot sorted by row/col, selected identity, chart editability/CSV names and paths or image name/path. It calls slots.select; existing-asset drop resolves draggableAsset and calls connectToSlot with explicit target slot ID. External drop separately invokes importToSlot. These summaries need all relevant slot/chart/reference facts, not only the currently selected graph. |
+| `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js:640-655,1082-1122` | readTrash summary gates empty-trash button via `.hasContents`; modal retains `.referenceCount` as UI-local confirmation data; action invokes emptyTrash, which re-resolves current trash on command. A canonical trash subtree may expose descendants but is not the current count summary. Removing the warning or inventing a count lookup is not authorized. |
+| `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js:663-692,1123-1215` | Move picker/confirmation consumes current moveOptions/planMove collision, destination, uniqueName, enteringTrash and count. The previously deferred `result.trashed` null-result interpretation at `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js:668` remains unchanged; this unit does not define its success/reset semantics. |
+| `sourcecode/frontend/mantine_ui.js:1349-1391` (`FastFigureGraphDataEditor`) | readTree `.data` supplies all CSV option IDs/names; graphs.readData independently supplies current selected chart/CSV/columns. A nested-tree migration must preserve asset identity/choice and independent valid CSV selection, not replace it with the selected graph object's CSV. This adjacent actual tree-read consumer belongs in the same shape translation. |
+
+No new long-lived tree snapshot, general mutation candidate, callback or Backend access in Frontend was introduced. Existing row/import/slot/drop behavior was inspected for dependency mapping, not declared fully correct or executed.
+
+## Existing official reads: available and insufficient facts
+
+- `assets.readTree`/`assets.readTrash`: authoritative canonical relationship/subtree is specified, but not `.charts`/`.slots` summary fields or a count envelope. Returning the old flat summary under these names is not a valid interpretation.
+- `assets.readDeletionTarget`: explicit per-asset target/count/owner meaning exists upstream; current public wrapper narrows it to selected identity/count. Even upstream it returns none for a directory, so it does not directly give trash-root aggregate confirmation. Adapting arbitrary-path calls/aggregating counts still requires an authorized public/caller correspondence, not a hidden Backend call from Mantine.
+- `slots.readSelected`: only current selected visible slot identity/geometry/content. `graphs.readData`, `graphs.readLayout`, `graphs.readPalette`: selected owner reads (explicit chart ID in readData is for Application postcommit use), not all-slot summary APIs. Selecting each slot just to read is not allowed; that would mutate Frontend selection and change semantics.
+- `layout.readState`: current grid/style/visible slot geometry and preview plus session zoom, specified at `sourcescript/backend/project_state.py:313`, `sourcescript/application/public_api/layout_annotations.py:110-120`, `pseudocode/application/public_api/layout_annotations.pcal:83-92`. It does not specify the full all-chart CSV IDs/editability/assets reference-summary mapping used here.
+- Backend renderer/export projections do contain richer same-source content (`sourcescript/backend/project_state.py:347-364`; `pseudocode/backend/project_state.pcal:615-649`), but they are task-specific reads, not new public Mantine dependencies. Exposing them directly, querying generic export as a UI store, or calling Backend queries from Mantine would circumvent the declared boundary.
+
+Bounded exact-name/content searches across all `sourcescript` and `pseudocode` for `projectDataTreeObjects|projectDataTreeSnapshot|csvReferences|hasContents|referenceCount|readTree|readTrash` found canonical-tree/subtree contracts and per-asset/move reference counts, not an all-slot/chart UI-summary contract. Full relevant public assets/boundary and Mantine Source/PlusCal plus Backend VFS read/cascade contracts were inspected directly. No absence claim is based only on helper-name similarity or existing tests.
+
+## Required upstream input, not a selected design
+
+Before the coherent runtime unit can continue, the authority owner must specify how the retained UI obtains:
+
+1. All visible slot identities/ordering/content references and each owning chart's editability/real CSV references, preserving conversion exclusion and repeated reference counts.
+2. CSV readability/row-count metadata and image/CSV display identity alongside the canonical tree, without changing canonical parent/order semantics.
+3. Empty-trash nonempty detection and aggregate reference confirmation using the same real-reference set as cascade; specify the official public read/caller adaptation and read-time scope. Existing selected-only deletion wrapper is not a drop-in aggregate.
+4. Exact public/caller shape correspondence: whether existing explicit reads are sufficient after a specified adaptation/composition, or an upstream-defined public projection is needed. If any product behavior is intentionally removed/changed, that requires an explicit upstream decision rather than worker omission.
+
+These are options/questions for the authority owner, not permission to add a summary API, tree envelope or new domain branch. Any new meaning must start in Source, close there and propagate through PlusCal before runtime translation. The current canonical tree/trash meaning itself is not proposed for reversal to match JS.
+
